4,1,,status,Misaki,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":5,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
5,1,1,talk,Misaki,,We should prioritize how these changes affect the staff. I'm concerned about the actual workload during implementation.,"{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
6,1,1,talk,Kenji,,I agree! But we also need to make sure the new system actually works in the yards. It can't just be good on paper.,"{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
7,1,1,talk,Toshio,,We must look beyond the initial quote. I want to understand the long-term financial commitments and how the board views these requests.,"{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
8,1,1,talk,Yumi,,I want to make sure we have clear ownership when things go wrong! And that the system can actually keep up with our business changes.,"{""words"":25,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
9,1,1,talk,Benjamin,,"A prudent approach, indeed. I suspect we should examine how previous transitions were handled to avoid inheriting a legacy of ""quick fixes.""","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
10,1,2,talk,Misaki,,"@Toshio, financial patterns are important, but if the people are too stretched to use the system, the investment is wasted.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
11,1,2,talk,Kenji,,"Exactly! If the depot floor is in chaos during peak season, the fanciest software won't save us. We need to check the calendar.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
12,1,2,talk,Toshio,,"I acknowledge that, but operational failure often stems from underfunded maintenance. I'll be looking at the renewal invoices.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
13,1,2,talk,Yumi,,"That's a good point, Toshio-san! But I'm really worried about who takes the lead during a crisis. I'll check the outage ownership.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
14,1,2,talk,Benjamin,,I shall focus on the technical longevity. I'm curious about the upgrade history and how we handled the data lift in 2018.,"{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
15,1,3,talk,Misaki,,I'll look into the administrator retirements and the last rollout to see how the burden was distributed.,"{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
16,1,3,talk,Kenji,,I'm going to check the yard devices and the peak-season cutover. We can't afford a crash when the freight is piling up!,"{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
17,1,3,talk,Toshio,,I will also examine the board minutes. I want to see where the gap lies between requested and approved capital.,"{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
18,1,3,talk,Yumi,,I'll also look at the warehouse rule changes! I want to see if the system actually adapted when new accounts were added.,"{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
19,1,3,talk,Benjamin,,It seems we have a comprehensive list. I'll stick with the upgrade history and the 2018 pay move data lift.,"{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
