30,2,,status,Toshio,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":1,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
31,2,,status,Yumi,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":2,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
32,2,,status,Benjamin,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":3,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
33,2,,status,Kenji,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":4,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
34,2,,status,Misaki,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":5,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
35,2,1,talk,Misaki,,"My findings are worrying. We are losing key knowledge, and the last rollout's training didn't actually stick with the supervisors.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,Kenji,,That's scary! I found out our yard equipment is a total mess and we have zero breathing room during peak season.,"{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,Toshio,,I've noticed a pattern. The board ignores the long-term operating costs as long as the initial capital request looks small.,"{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,Yumi,,Oh no! I found that nobody was actually in charge during the last outage. Everyone just pointed fingers at each other!,"{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Benjamin,,How charming. I've discovered we have a habit of letting systems age into obsolescence and paying outsiders for data moves that they don't actually finish.,"{""words"":25,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Misaki,,"@Yumi, if ownership is fragmented, the overworked staff will be the ones forced to fix things on their own time.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[""Yumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Kenji,,"Right! And if the software doesn't play nice with our old yard devices, the guys on the floor will just go back to using paper.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,Toshio,,"The real danger is the ""hidden"" bill. I've seen that add-on licenses climb every year while the main contract stays flat.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,Yumi,,Exactly! And I saw that the business rules changed almost immediately after the last project started. We need a system that can bend!,"{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Benjamin,,"It seems we are trapped between a rock and a hard place: a system that is too rigid to change, or a ""flexible"" one that is a patchwork of external repairs.","{""words"":31,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Misaki,,We need a vendor that provides heavy on-site support. We can't rely on a manual or a remote help desk right now.,"{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Kenji,,I agree with Misaki! We need someone who knows that the depot doesn't stop moving just because we're installing a new update.,"{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""Misaki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,Toshio,,"I will prioritize a vendor with a predictable, all-inclusive cost model. I cannot support another system with creeping annual fees.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,Yumi,,"I'll be looking for a vendor who takes full accountability for the outcome, not just the installation. No more finger-pointing!","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Benjamin,,"Logic suggests we avoid any vendor that relies solely on ""lift and shift"" migrations. We need a clean break from these lingering errors.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
