60,3,1,talk,Misaki,,I strongly prefer Anchor. Having an engineering team present through the rollout is the only way to ensure the staff actually adopts it.,"{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
61,3,1,talk,Kenji,,I'm with Misaki! Anchor sounds like the only one that will actually survive the depot floor and the peak season chaos.,"{""words"":21,""mentions"":[""Misaki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,1,talk,Toshio,,Corvus is a nightmare waiting to happen. Modular licenses mean separate bills and creeping costs. I prefer the fixed nature of Meridian.,"{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,1,talk,Yumi,,"Meridian sounds a bit too rigid with a ""fixed configuration."" I'm worried it won't adapt when our business rules change next month!","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,1,talk,Benjamin,,"Corvus is indeed a recipe for fragmentation. However, Tessera's reliance on a ""partner firm"" for migration reminds me too much of our 2018 disaster.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,2,talk,Misaki,,"@Toshio, Meridian's regional service team isn't the same as having engineers on-site. We can't risk another training failure.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,2,talk,Kenji,,"Exactly! If the yard devices fail, I want an Anchor engineer right there to fix it, not a ""regional team"" on a phone call.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,2,talk,Toshio,,"While on-site support is valuable, Anchor's on-premise deployment means we bear the long-term hardware and maintenance costs. Meridian's hosted model is more predictable.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,2,talk,Yumi,,"But @Toshio-san, if we go with Meridian and it breaks, who is in charge? A ""regional team"" sounds like more finger-pointing!","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,2,talk,Benjamin,,"Anchor's on-premise approach is a double-edged sword. It avoids the ""cloud"" abstraction, but we've already proven we are terrible at maintaining our own racks.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
70,3,3,talk,Misaki,,"We are already understaffed. We can't maintain the servers, but we can't afford to fail the rollout. Anchor's engineers bridge that gap.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
71,3,3,talk,Kenji,,"I'll take the server risk over the risk of the depot stopping. Anchor is the only one that feels ""industrial"" enough for us.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
72,3,3,talk,Toshio,,I cannot ignore the financial risk of on-premise hardware and the potential for hidden maintenance costs. Meridian is the safest financial bet.,"{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
73,3,3,talk,Yumi,,"I'm torn, but I think Anchor is the best for accountability. If they are on-site, they can't point fingers at someone else!","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
74,3,3,talk,Benjamin,,"If we must choose between a hosted system that might be too rigid and an on-premise system we might neglect, I'll choose the one with the most direct accountability.","{""words"":29,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
75,3,4,talk,Misaki,,It seems we are leaning toward Anchor. It's the only way to protect the people who are already stretched too thin.,"{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
76,3,4,talk,Kenji,,Yes! Let's go with Anchor. It's the only one that won't break the moment it hits the yard.,"{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
77,3,4,talk,Toshio,,"I still have reservations about the long-term cost of on-premise, but I see the consensus. I will vote for my preference.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
78,3,4,talk,Yumi,,I'm so happy we're thinking about the people and the accountability! I'm voting for Anchor!,"{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
79,3,4,talk,Benjamin,,"A rational choice, given our history of neglecting internal updates. Let us hope the engineers are as capable as they claim.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
